 {"id":"fabro-e6df","title":"gofib: add README with usage and flag reference","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T11:38:40.410Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T11:47:51.762Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA README.md at the repo root that documents the gofib CLI: what it is\n(Go CLI printing Fibonacci numbers), install/build via mise/just,\nusage, and the full flag reference.\n\n## Flag reference to cover\n\n- `-n <int>`: how many numbers to print (default 100, must be >= 1)\n- `-json`: JSON Lines output, one object per number (`{\"index\":<int>,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}`)\n- `-pretty`: aligned column output\n- `-version`: print version and exit\n\nUse the vocabulary from CONTEXT.md (text mode, JSON mode, count flag).\nShow real example invocations and their actual output — run the built\nbinary to capture it, do not invent output.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- README.md exists at the repo root\n- Examples match actual binary behavior\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T11:47:51.762Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-4f3e","title":"gofib: add -start flag to begin printing at a given index","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T14:23:57.517Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T14:23:57.517Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-start <int>` flag: the first Fibonacci index to print. Default 0.\nCombines with `-n` (how many), `-json`, and `-pretty`.\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-start 10 -n 5` prints indices 10..14 in the active output mode\n  (text mode line format stays `<index>: <value>`).\n- Validation mirrors the `-n` contract: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error message.\n- `-start` must not change what `-n` counts (still the number of lines).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag parsed via the flag package; `Fib(n)` stays the only computation\n  (no inline recomputation — see CONTEXT.md).\n- Table-driven tests: default start, start+n combination, start with\n  -json and -pretty, negative start rejected.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-start` row; example invocation with\n  REAL output captured from the built binary (do not invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green"}
